                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Telegram, Field Marshal Commander in-Chief of Allied
                        Armies (D.G.C.R.A.) to President C.I.P.A., Spa</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3790/C.R.</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">G.Q.G.A., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-31">31 January, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A continuation of telegram No. 3564/C.R. and in reply to telegram 496 of the 27th
                    January.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>First, the arrangements made by the German Government to allow the passage
                        of food into Poland are noted.</item>
                    <pb facs="1000" n="990" xml:id="pg990"/>
                    <item>Secondly, it is noted that the rolling material supplied by the Germans
                        for the transport of these provisions shall be immediately returned.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>P.O. The Director General of C.R.A.<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Payot</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
